      "  > Comparative Advantage: This model is slightly better than a basic text-only therapist because it maintains a supportive tone and attempts to engage the client in reflection. However, it falls short in utilizing emotional metadata effectively, as it does not significantly enhance the understanding of the client's underlying emotions or guide the client towards deeper insights. The therapist's responses were somewhat generic and did not fully leverage potential non-verbal cues to uncover deeper emotional layers.\n",
