      "  > Comparative Advantage: This model is better than a basic text-only therapist because it effectively captures the emotional subtext and latent concerns of the client, even without explicit metadata. The therapist was able to identify and address the client's fears and vulnerabilities, which a text-only model might miss. However, the therapist could have utilized potential metadata, such as emotional valence or arousal cues, to further enhance their understanding and intervention strategies. Overall, the therapist's ability to perceive and respond to the client's emotional subtext was strong, but there is room for improvement in uncovering deeper latent concerns.\n",
