      "  > Comparative Advantage: This model is better than a basic text-only therapist as it effectively uses the client's verbal cues to maintain a supportive and empathetic environment. However, without metadata, the therapist missed opportunities to explore deeper emotional subtext, such as the client's fear of vulnerability and past experiences. The therapist could have benefited from metadata indicating emotional valence or arousal to better address these underlying issues.\n",
